projects.description:
Support community empowerment initiatives to uphold sexual and reproductive rights and to diminish sexual and gender based violence. Specifically, the interventions will include:

- Building capacity of community leaders (elders, traditional leaders, religious leaders) to be able to engaged in addressing discriminatory practices, including harmful practices such as VAWC;
- Building the capacity of community members in selected Shehia &amp; Wards to engage on legislation &amp; policy dialogue to prevent and respond to VAWC; 
- Communities dialogues on legislation and policy to prevent and respond to VAWC in selected districts;
- Community mobilization and awareness raising;
- Women and girls empowerment and protection programmes;
- Building capacity of host communities and refugees to respond to sexual and gender based violence (Kigoma);
- From the year 2020/2021, engaging communities on VAWC and harmful practices in the aftermath of the Covid-19 outbreak.

TA and FA  to Agriculture Sector Line Ministries (ASLM), agencies and institutions to review and/or formulate socio-economic policies, strategies and plans, with a focus on decent rural employment/work in the Agriculture sector. This activity involves the implementation of the formulated and/or revised policies on the ground. Therefore,the new formulations and/or revisions will goes hand in hand with the implementation of activities for a greater outreach to  beneficiaries and practical implementation of the decent work agenda. FAO is currently supporting the following policy/strategy works;  

1. Revised National Strategy for Youth Involvement in Agriculture ( NSYIA)  for mainland and Translate 	
2. Improved coordination between public, private and civil society youth development actors and young agri-entrepreneurs (Y-AWG)

TA to build capacities of Agriculture Sector Line Ministries (ASLM), agencies and institutions to bring timely and actionable agrometeorological information to farmers to reduce their uncertainty and improve their abilities to be resilient under changing weather patterns. Under this project, FAO is converting Agrometeorological data and analyses into timely and actionable information available to farmers. Specific outputs are;
  Trained cadres on how to develop and use agrometeorological information products; 
  Developed agro-meteorological information products (climatological analyses, downscaling weather forecasts, bulletins and info briefs) and disseminate via ICT; 
  Convened forums for awareness raising and sharing of agrometeorological information products with guidance on how to respond to the forecasts.
